WEBVTT

00:18:59.011 --> 00:19:01.097
and out into the public sphere.

00:19:01.628 --> 00:19:04.454
There's a related worldview

00:19:04.478 --> 00:19:07.284
that in some ways
isn't all that different from yours,

00:19:07.308 --> 00:19:09.794
which is this idea of memes

00:19:09.818 --> 00:19:14.632
that Richard Dawkins first wrote about
30 years ago, I want to say.

00:19:14.656 --> 00:19:17.390
The word "meme" has been
sort of co-opted on the internet

00:19:17.414 --> 00:19:21.836
to mean often sort of
silly little pictures or GIFs

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:24.923
that get passed around
and explode to lots of views,

00:19:24.947 --> 00:19:27.987
but the original idea behind a meme
is much broader than that.

00:19:28.011 --> 00:19:32.201
It's anything that can be reproduced
in a mind and spread,